Purposes and legal bases: the core, contact and appointment data needed to prepare and carry out the tattoo appointment are processed on the basis of Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. For the health information used in preparation, the personal preliminary conversation and documentation, we obtain explicit consent under Art. 6(1)(a) and Art. 9(2)(a) GDPR. Tattoo photos for the portfolio and the stated websites are only used with separate, voluntary consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).

Where further retention is needed to assert, exercise or defend legal claims, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR applies, and for health data additionally Art. 9(2)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest is the necessary proof of the information given and consent obtained, or legal action or defence. This does not amount to unlimited storage.

Retention and deletion: {{studio.retention}}

Access, recipients and filing: {{studio.recipients}}

Withdrawal: a consent given can be withdrawn at any time for the future, verbally with the owner or via the email address stated above. Processing carried out before the withdrawal remains lawful. From the withdrawal onward, processing on the basis of this consent ends. Any further, independent retention only takes place where another legal basis exists, and only to the extent necessary.

Your rights: subject to the legal requirements, you have rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability. You can object to processing based on legitimate interests for reasons arising from your particular situation. You can complain to the data protection supervisory authority responsible for your studio. The studio needs to add the responsible authority.

Required and voluntary information: providing the health information is not a legal requirement. Please only share details relevant to the agreed tattoo. If information needed for safe performance is missing, this must be clarified in the personal preliminary conversation; the tattoo may not be able to go ahead as a result. Photo consent is voluntary; declining it has no disadvantages for the tattoo. There is no automated decision-making or profiling.

The app processes your details and your signature on this device and creates the PDF locally. It does not transmit this customer data to the internet. Form entries not yet completed are lost on closing or reloading. When the signed PDF is created, name, tattoo appointment, artist, total price and any deposit are additionally stored in a local income overview. This is used to track and evaluate the agreed services; health information and signatures are not stored in it. This contract and billing data is processed to perform the contract under Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. Access to, backup of and any required deletion of this overview are the owner's responsibility. The signed PDF is additionally kept as a copy in the app's storage on this device until the studio deletes this copy; it is not transmitted. The studio is responsible for filing, accessing and retaining the saved PDF files.
